WEBVTT

00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:12.930
Let's eat!

00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:19.430
Wonder what that's about.

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:23.850
Delicious!

00:00:23.850 --> 00:00:25.600
A surprising announcement on Hanamura Neon.

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:30.540
It's been verified that the singer, Hanamura Neon-san, is in the company of a young woman.

00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:37.660
There have been eye-witnesses who have recently spotted the two of them together in the RPG Building where Hanamura-san lives.

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:44.160
Y-Yoshino?!

00:00:56.030 --> 00:00:58.220
This is the worst.

00:01:14.420 --> 00:01:15.950
Wh-what do you want?

00:01:15.950 --> 00:01:17.810
You're in the way! Move!

00:01:18.670 --> 00:01:19.630
Yoshino!

00:01:19.630 --> 00:01:20.120
Y-Yes?!

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:22.050
What's the meaning of this?

00:01:22.050 --> 00:01:24.200
How did you, the meekest of us all among DATS's members...

00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:27.750
Manage to snag Hanamura Neon?!

00:01:28.160 --> 00:01:29.880
Er, well...

00:01:29.880 --> 00:01:31.240
Explain yourself!

00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:33.460
Who cares who she goes out with.

00:01:34.610 --> 00:01:36.370
It's not like that's complicating the missions.

00:01:36.370 --> 00:01:38.040
Yes, it is!

00:01:36.370 --> 00:01:38.040
Yes, it is!

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:42.120
We've been getting phone calls one after another since morning!

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:46.000
We're also getting loads of hate mail from Neon's fans!

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:49.030
They're demanding to know who Fujieda Yoshino thinks she is!

00:01:49.030 --> 00:01:49.940
No way!

00:01:50.550 --> 00:01:53.160
They didn't say my name on TV!

00:01:53.370 --> 00:01:55.650
No, everything's exposed.

00:02:00.410 --> 00:02:05.830
Your name, birthday, the address where you work, even your blood type.

00:02:06.610 --> 00:02:08.310
This is the worst.

00:02:08.310 --> 00:02:09.500
That's a bad picture!

00:02:10.580 --> 00:02:13.160
Now, confess! When and where...

00:02:13.160 --> 00:02:14.500
Did you first get to know Neon?

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:16.480
W-Well...

00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:19.090
Let me explain.

00:02:19.090 --> 00:02:19.930
Captain!

00:02:24.770 --> 00:02:25.900
Thank you.

00:02:30.230 --> 00:02:35.030
A month ago, a Digimon signal appeared in the RPG Building.

00:02:35.030 --> 00:02:36.670
Analysis established that...

00:02:36.670 --> 00:02:39.990
The Digimon concealed there is Keramon.

00:02:40.450 --> 00:02:45.970
That's a Digimon who interpositions itself in the Internet and freely controls a variety of mechanical devices, correct?

00:02:45.970 --> 00:02:46.840
That's right.

00:02:46.840 --> 00:02:51.920
DATS's second division scouted the area secretly, and our prime suspect was revealed to be...

00:02:52.410 --> 00:02:54.380
Hanamura Neon.

00:02:55.130 --> 00:02:57.340
So he's harboring a Digimon...

00:02:57.870 --> 00:03:00.400
We're not certain about that yet.

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:01.180
Yes.

00:03:01.620 --> 00:03:05.240
That's why I had Yoshino perform an undercover investigation.

00:03:05.240 --> 00:03:06.900
What's an undercover investigation?

00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:08.350
That's when you sneak around to investigate.

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:13.650
But if there's a Digimon signal, we should just step in and arrest it right away.

00:03:13.650 --> 00:03:16.180
We can't.

00:03:16.180 --> 00:03:18.360
The RPG Building is hi-tech.

00:03:18.970 --> 00:03:21.830
It has the latest advancements in its security system.

00:03:21.830 --> 00:03:25.880
So if we carelessly break in, we'll be kicked out before we know it.

00:03:25.880 --> 00:03:27.000
I see.

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:29.410
We'll leave Yoshino to continue her investigation for now.

00:03:29.410 --> 00:03:31.270
The rest of you will assist her.

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:33.380
I can't agree with that!

00:03:34.230 --> 00:03:36.150
Why does it have to be Yoshino?

00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:39.330
If all you have to do is get close to Neon, we could have...!

00:03:39.330 --> 00:03:40.760
Well, wait.

00:03:40.760 --> 00:03:43.870
There's a reason why I assigned her to this mission.

00:03:44.180 --> 00:03:46.930
Neon is my childhood friend.

00:03:48.730 --> 00:03:50.820
We were in the same class in elementary school.

00:03:50.820 --> 00:03:52.300
It's the first time I've heard that.

00:03:52.300 --> 00:03:55.930
Why did you keep quiet about something that important?

00:03:55.930 --> 00:03:57.600
Is it really that important?

00:03:57.600 --> 00:03:59.530
He's completely different from before.

00:03:59.530 --> 00:04:03.270
He was shorter than me, and he was fat.

00:04:03.270 --> 00:04:06.110
When he debuted, I didn't recognize him at all.

00:04:09.150 --> 00:04:10.030
Hey!

00:04:11.750 --> 00:04:12.580
Hanamura Neon!

00:04:14.950 --> 00:04:16.020
Hitoshi!

00:04:17.530 --> 00:04:18.890
Hitoshi?

00:04:19.850 --> 00:04:22.210
I told you not to call me by my real name.

00:04:22.760 --> 00:04:24.490
What does it matter?

00:04:24.490 --> 00:04:26.720
You haven't changed at all.

00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:27.580
See you later then.

00:04:27.580 --> 00:04:28.450
Okay!

00:04:28.450 --> 00:04:29.290
See you!

00:04:30.600 --> 00:04:31.540
What's that?

00:04:31.540 --> 00:04:32.850
They're lovey-dovey for each other.

00:04:32.850 --> 00:04:34.230
Is this really a mission?

00:04:38.040 --> 00:04:39.810
What was that "Hitoshi" thing about?

00:04:39.810 --> 00:04:42.200
Tell us everything!

00:04:43.580 --> 00:04:44.420
Ow!

00:04:46.760 --> 00:04:47.950
But Yoshino...

00:04:47.950 --> 00:04:48.930
No,

00:04:48.930 --> 00:04:50.240
he's a nice guy.

00:04:50.240 --> 00:04:52.870
There's no way he can do anything bad.

00:05:05.930 --> 00:05:06.470
What?

00:05:06.470 --> 00:05:07.720
The carrots.

00:05:07.720 --> 00:05:10.300
I was just thinking that you're finally able to eat them now.

00:05:10.300 --> 00:05:11.110
Huh?

00:05:11.330 --> 00:05:16.390
Whenever we had carrots for lunch, you'd always leave them behind and the teacher would get so mad about it.

00:05:16.940 --> 00:05:20.510
Whenever you were on-duty, you'd purposely give me a heap of them.

00:05:20.510 --> 00:05:23.900
I was exercising parental love because I wanted you to eat healthy and get bigger.

00:05:24.640 --> 00:05:26.190
It's a pretty big parental love you have.

00:05:29.410 --> 00:05:33.220
I remember you were never able to do anything on your own...

00:05:33.220 --> 00:05:34.300
Thanks for the meal.

00:05:34.820 --> 00:05:36.090
Want me to make some coffee?

00:05:36.280 --> 00:05:37.360
No thanks.

00:05:37.360 --> 00:05:38.580
I have work to do.

00:05:38.990 --> 00:05:40.780
Hey, show me your work.

00:05:40.780 --> 00:05:41.520
I can't.

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:43.920
I won't be able to come up with a good phrase if I'm distracted.

00:05:43.920 --> 00:05:45.750
Oh, but...

00:05:45.750 --> 00:05:46.770
That's how it is.

00:05:47.420 --> 00:05:50.290
So you can't come into my room, okay?

00:05:56.100 --> 00:05:58.770
Yoshino, it's time for us to get to work, too.

00:05:58.770 --> 00:05:59.280
Yeah.

00:06:00.510 --> 00:06:03.690
Samples of his new song have been downloaded by more than 7 million people.

00:06:03.690 --> 00:06:05.520
Here's Hanamura Neon-san!

00:06:05.520 --> 00:06:07.240
Thank you. This is all thanks to my fans.

00:06:07.980 --> 00:06:11.910
I've heard that you've gotten a girlfriend recently.

00:06:12.350 --> 00:06:13.950
Masaru-niichan, I can't see!

00:06:14.620 --> 00:06:18.350
She's a great encouragement to me in creating my songs.

00:06:18.350 --> 00:06:21.670
But because she's an ordinary person, please leave her be.

00:06:22.320 --> 00:06:24.380
Neon is so cool!

00:06:24.380 --> 00:06:25.320
What part of him?

00:06:28.300 --> 00:06:32.090
Obviously, the part where he tries so hard to protect his girlfriend.

00:06:32.500 --> 00:06:38.070
I'm sure that some day now, there'll be someone who'll cherish me just like him.

00:06:38.480 --> 00:06:39.880
So, with that in mind, here!

00:06:39.880 --> 00:06:40.390
What's this?

00:06:41.010 --> 00:06:45.000
I heard that Yoshino-oneechan's going out with Neon!

00:06:41.010 --> 00:06:46.490
NOTE: <i>Oneechan</i> (お姉ちゃん) is a familiar add-on for an older female.

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:46.490
How'd you know that?

00:06:50.690 --> 00:06:51.740
It was you!

00:06:52.410 --> 00:06:56.690
C'mon! Ask Yoshino-oneechan to get me his autograph!

00:06:56.690 --> 00:06:57.460
No!

00:06:57.460 --> 00:06:58.500
Why?!

00:06:58.500 --> 00:07:03.250
Look Chika, you wouldn't like it if other people were prying about who you like or date, right?

00:07:04.480 --> 00:07:05.710
It's the same with Yoshino.

00:07:05.710 --> 00:07:09.550
That's to say nothing of the fact that you're demanding his autograph just because he's a celebrity...

00:07:10.390 --> 00:07:12.520
Masaru-niichan, you're stingy.

00:07:14.310 --> 00:07:15.950
Hey Chika, wait!

00:07:15.950 --> 00:07:17.380
You made her cry.

00:07:18.210 --> 00:07:20.490
It's <i>your</i>  fault!

00:07:22.970 --> 00:07:24.940
Now, let's get started.

00:07:26.360 --> 00:07:36.160
Keramon

00:07:26.360 --> 00:07:36.160
Child Level

00:07:26.900 --> 00:07:27.890
Keramon.

00:07:27.890 --> 00:07:31.990
A Child Level Digimon that consumes a massive amount of data with its large mouth.

00:07:31.990 --> 00:07:33.860
Its special attack is Crazy Giggle.

00:07:33.860 --> 00:07:36.160
It can shoot a destructive ball of light from its mouth.

00:08:13.680 --> 00:08:14.960
What's this?

00:08:14.960 --> 00:08:16.520
Neon's promotion?

00:08:25.450 --> 00:08:26.300
Huh?

00:08:26.300 --> 00:08:27.040
What's wrong?

00:08:31.240 --> 00:08:32.460
I thought I turned it off...

00:08:36.030 --> 00:08:37.760
Did it break?

00:08:37.760 --> 00:08:38.660
What?

00:08:39.060 --> 00:08:40.300
What the hell?

00:08:42.160 --> 00:08:43.100
This is weird.

00:09:58.010 --> 00:10:01.600
Yoshino Gets Her Cinderella Story?!

00:09:58.010 --> 00:10:01.600
Chrysalimon's Shadow

00:09:58.330 --> 00:10:00.300
Yoshino Gets Her Cinderella Story?!

00:10:00.300 --> 00:10:01.600
Chrysalimon's Shadow!

00:10:17.060 --> 00:10:18.070
Captain!

00:10:18.070 --> 00:10:19.430
What's going on here?

00:10:19.430 --> 00:10:20.560
It's a web hijacking.

00:10:21.550 --> 00:10:23.740
Hanamura Neon's promotional video is...

00:10:23.740 --> 00:10:25.450
being distributed indiscriminately to all computer networks.

00:10:25.450 --> 00:10:26.910
What about our transmitters?

00:10:27.560 --> 00:10:29.430
I'm unable to make any analysis.

00:10:33.260 --> 00:10:34.810
Where's Yoshino?

00:10:34.810 --> 00:10:37.340
I've been trying to contact her, but I'm getting no answer.

00:10:37.800 --> 00:10:38.550
Keep trying!

00:10:39.900 --> 00:10:40.650
Masaru!

00:10:42.290 --> 00:10:44.350
Aniki, wait up!

00:10:49.810 --> 00:10:52.730
I don't feel any signs of life coming from this room.

00:10:53.510 --> 00:10:57.410
It might have a special screen around it that nullifies all data.

00:11:12.550 --> 00:11:14.430
Hey! Where did you come from?!

00:11:14.430 --> 00:11:15.170
Let go of me!

00:11:15.780 --> 00:11:16.590
Masaru?

00:11:18.950 --> 00:11:20.270
You're breaking and entering!

00:11:20.270 --> 00:11:21.220
Come with me!

00:11:21.220 --> 00:11:22.680
Yoshino, you're in there, right?!

00:11:23.110 --> 00:11:24.060
I said, come with me!

00:11:24.060 --> 00:11:25.100
Answer me!

00:11:25.340 --> 00:11:27.390
Stay still, you little...!

00:11:29.330 --> 00:11:30.240
Yoshino!

00:11:31.820 --> 00:11:33.480
Good, you're okay!

00:11:33.920 --> 00:11:36.040
Masaru! What are you...?

00:11:36.040 --> 00:11:37.170
Did something happen?

00:11:37.170 --> 00:11:38.350
Don't play dumb!

00:11:38.350 --> 00:11:39.900
This was all a part of your scheme!

00:11:39.900 --> 00:11:41.520
Wh-What are you doing?

00:11:41.520 --> 00:11:42.200
Who are you?!

00:11:42.730 --> 00:11:45.240
What are you plotting, using that Digimon?!

00:11:45.760 --> 00:11:47.340
What are you talking about?!

00:11:47.340 --> 00:11:49.090
Don't act like you don't know!

00:11:49.090 --> 00:11:50.060
Stop it!

00:11:52.700 --> 00:11:54.920
How dare you suddenly intrude into other people's houses!

00:11:55.790 --> 00:11:58.670
Why don't you consider <i>not</i>  being a nuisance to others for a change?

00:11:58.670 --> 00:11:59.720
What?!

00:12:00.250 --> 00:12:01.250
I'm sorry about this.

00:12:01.250 --> 00:12:02.410
It's okay.

00:12:02.410 --> 00:12:03.620
I'll come back later.

00:12:07.490 --> 00:12:08.350
See you.

00:12:10.110 --> 00:12:10.890
Hey, wait!

00:12:11.890 --> 00:12:12.970
I said, wait!

00:12:13.890 --> 00:12:15.350
What was that for?

00:12:15.950 --> 00:12:16.840
Idiot.

00:12:16.840 --> 00:12:18.820
You're ruining my undercover investigation.

00:12:19.830 --> 00:12:22.420
What the hell, I was just worried about her.

00:12:22.420 --> 00:12:23.050
Hey, you.

00:12:25.680 --> 00:12:27.440
Why don't you come with me to the office?

00:12:27.440 --> 00:12:28.740
N-No thanks!

00:12:34.060 --> 00:12:36.780
It's too dark, you can't even tell who it is!

00:12:36.780 --> 00:12:38.770
You call yourself a professional?!

00:12:39.100 --> 00:12:42.150
I couldn't exactly use the flash back there...

00:12:42.150 --> 00:12:45.380
This type of shot's not good enough to publish anyway!

00:12:45.380 --> 00:12:48.490
B-But if I do any more than this, it'll become a crime!

00:12:48.490 --> 00:12:49.470
You moron!

00:12:50.150 --> 00:12:53.080
It's because we're walking that very thin line that it makes our readers happy!

00:12:53.080 --> 00:12:54.730
Get a shot of something more extreme!

00:12:55.060 --> 00:12:57.290
You're not the only cameraman I've got!

00:12:57.290 --> 00:12:59.410
U-Understood! I'll do it!

00:13:03.820 --> 00:13:06.240
The Digimon's signal first showed up a month ago.

00:13:06.670 --> 00:13:11.740
The number of downloads for Neon's new song has been rapidly increasing since then.

00:13:12.800 --> 00:13:16.000
Do you think the Digimon is deliberately manipulating things?

00:13:16.000 --> 00:13:18.040
I believe it's a good possibility.

00:13:18.460 --> 00:13:19.980
So that's why yesterday...

00:13:20.350 --> 00:13:22.500
It appears we must choose what to do now all the more.

00:13:23.170 --> 00:13:25.540
We should approach Hanamura Neon's residence straight away.

00:13:25.540 --> 00:13:26.530
Yes.

00:13:26.530 --> 00:13:28.120
So we're breaking in?!

00:13:28.120 --> 00:13:29.280
Wait, please!

00:13:29.940 --> 00:13:31.970
We still don't have any evidence!

00:13:33.330 --> 00:13:34.470
What's Neon's schedule?

00:13:35.090 --> 00:13:37.460
At 12 PM, he'll be appearing on a live television program.

00:13:37.460 --> 00:13:39.840
Afterwards, at 3 PM, he'll be going back to his professional work.

00:13:39.840 --> 00:13:42.980
At 12 AM, he has plans to appear on a radio talk show.

00:13:43.960 --> 00:13:46.730
Tonight, I'll allow a coercive investigation to be carried out.

00:13:46.730 --> 00:13:47.940
Tohma will take command.

00:13:49.230 --> 00:13:50.160
I have a request.

00:13:51.060 --> 00:13:52.870
Please take Yoshino off the investigation.

00:13:53.470 --> 00:13:54.560
Tohma?

00:13:55.150 --> 00:13:57.270
It's taboo for her personal feelings to get involved in this case.

00:13:57.270 --> 00:13:58.570
Very well.

00:13:58.570 --> 00:14:00.130
Yoshino, you will stay at headquarters.

00:14:00.130 --> 00:14:02.060
Everyone else will follow under Tohma.

00:14:02.060 --> 00:14:02.990
Roger!

00:14:02.060 --> 00:14:02.990
Roger!

00:14:07.670 --> 00:14:12.100
Once the time 12 AM is announced, we'll break in and secure the Digimon in hiding.

00:14:12.100 --> 00:14:12.850
Roger.

00:14:13.810 --> 00:14:15.490
Five minutes before the plan initiates.

00:14:15.490 --> 00:14:15.850
Wait!

00:14:18.370 --> 00:14:19.860
Yoshino's going in.

00:14:19.860 --> 00:14:20.270
Tohma!

00:14:20.270 --> 00:14:21.590
What do we do?

00:14:22.970 --> 00:14:26.990
Turn on the hidden mic I set on her, and let her go.

00:14:26.990 --> 00:14:27.530
Roger!

00:14:28.070 --> 00:14:29.420
Impressive as always, Master.

00:14:29.420 --> 00:14:30.610
You were expecting this.

00:14:31.100 --> 00:14:33.580
If you want to deceive your enemies, you must first deceive your friends, as they say.

00:14:39.080 --> 00:14:39.860
Yoshino...

00:14:42.420 --> 00:14:44.600
Yoshino, is this really okay?

00:14:44.600 --> 00:14:45.290
Yeah.

00:14:45.290 --> 00:14:47.230
I want to settle this personally.

00:14:50.550 --> 00:14:51.390
Yoshino!

00:14:51.390 --> 00:14:52.220
Let's go.

00:15:04.010 --> 00:15:06.440
So, you really want to know my secret that badly?

00:15:06.760 --> 00:15:07.980
Hitoshi...

00:15:07.980 --> 00:15:09.270
What are you doing here?

00:15:09.270 --> 00:15:11.350
Is that your Digimon?

00:15:11.350 --> 00:15:12.660
She's pretty cute.

00:15:12.990 --> 00:15:14.750
Why is Neon there?!

00:15:14.750 --> 00:15:16.330
He's supposed to be on radio right now!

00:15:17.800 --> 00:15:22.290
I've realized lately that there were some people snooping around me.

00:15:23.590 --> 00:15:26.250
That's why I made up a fake schedule and waited.

00:15:26.910 --> 00:15:29.710
To think that you were one of them...

00:15:30.370 --> 00:15:32.930
It's prohibited to be giving a Digimon refuge!

00:15:33.500 --> 00:15:34.760
Don't order me around!

00:15:46.210 --> 00:15:47.780
Let me introduce you!

00:15:47.780 --> 00:15:50.690
This is Keramon, the Digimon you're looking for!

00:15:51.240 --> 00:15:52.970
He's amazing!

00:15:52.970 --> 00:15:58.370
He distributes my songs all around the world, and he can freely rewrite the rankings!

00:15:59.900 --> 00:16:02.710
Right now, my name is known to everyone throughout the world!

00:16:03.200 --> 00:16:04.510
Hitoshi, stop this!

00:16:06.130 --> 00:16:07.170
Yoshino!

00:16:23.130 --> 00:16:23.920
Masaru!

00:16:23.920 --> 00:16:25.310
Baby Flame!

00:16:30.940 --> 00:16:32.400
Hand over the Digimon quietly!

00:16:32.760 --> 00:16:34.120
No way!

00:16:34.120 --> 00:16:36.600
Keramon is my partner!

00:16:36.600 --> 00:16:39.890
Thanks to him, my songs are played throughout the world!

00:16:39.890 --> 00:16:41.370
He's making me famous!

00:16:41.370 --> 00:16:43.140
You idiot!

00:16:45.030 --> 00:16:46.000
What are you doing?!

00:16:46.540 --> 00:16:48.620
What's this crap about him making you famous?!

00:16:48.620 --> 00:16:51.290
It's not through your own efforts!

00:16:51.290 --> 00:16:55.420
If you wanted to change yourself through your music, then do it using your own merit!

00:16:58.650 --> 00:17:00.290
This is an incredible scoop!

00:17:01.320 --> 00:17:02.150
He's...!

00:17:02.150 --> 00:17:03.010
Not good!

00:17:03.010 --> 00:17:03.700
Stop!

00:17:03.750 --> 00:17:04.800
Stop!

00:17:05.160 --> 00:17:09.290
Everyone needs to quit making fun of me!

00:17:10.910 --> 00:17:11.590
What's that?!

